{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Stolen waters are sweet, and bread of secrecy is pleasant</b> — a designation for transgressions and adultery done in secret, and everything forbidden, the inclination craves it more. And the reason: for by this the heart of the simpleton and the devoid-of-heart is seduced."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:21:46.957976051Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}